      "content": "HEMEL HEMPSTEAD 894/1/26                                HIGH STREET 18-JUN-48                               (West side) CHURCH OF ST MARY I Circa 1140-80 of flint rubble and Roman bricks with ashlar quoins, dressings and chancel vault.  Latin cross plan with crossing tower and C13 spire.  C14 south porch  C15 north porch and nave clerestory.  C14 brass in south aisle. 1841 monument to Sir Astley Paston Cooper.  1858 stained glass south chancel windows, Clayton and Bell  Vaulted north-east room, perhaps a sacristy, with east apse.  RCHM, p 109; VCH, p 225. Listing NGR: TL0550307813"
    }
